Cell[CellGroupData[{

Cell["\[VeryThinSpace]Conclusion", "Section",
 CellChangeTimes->{{3.9775359255386477`*^9, 3.977535927492813*^9}, {
  3.977916689905176*^9, 
  3.97791669019827*^9}},ExpressionUUID->"44078a61-e046-484d-88fb-\
bf9ffa1a9329"],

Cell["\<\
In this notebook, we derived the Schwarzschild metric for a static, \
spherically symmetric vacuum spacetime by constructing and employing a \
symbolic tensor calculator and compiler, \[ScriptCapitalU]\[ScriptCapitalD].\
\>", "Text",
 CellChangeTimes->{
  3.9782267679447403`*^9, {3.978227017829777*^9, 
   3.9782270629473143`*^9}},ExpressionUUID->"dea579b6-8891-4b19-b103-\
1c6b9c1409e5"],

Cell["\<\
The primary contribution of this work is the demonstration of the \
\[ScriptCapitalU]\[ScriptCapitalD] Toolkit (v1.8.0) as a viable prototype for \
automating calculations in general relativity. By separating the symbolic \
layer (abstract tensor notation, covariance, standard notations like comma, \
and Einstein summation) from the component layer (Wolfram arrays and \
differential equations), we achieved a readable and verifiable derivation.\
\>", "Text",
 CellChangeTimes->{
  3.9782267679447403`*^9, {3.978227017829777*^9, 
   3.978227169987425*^9}},ExpressionUUID->"74f6c55c-b3de-4137-85a3-\
a1013f64e294"],

Cell["Validation points include:", "Text",
 CellChangeTimes->{
  3.9782267679447403`*^9, {3.978227017829777*^9, 3.978227181755109*^9}, {
   3.978227379660836*^9, 
   3.978227381415834*^9}},ExpressionUUID->"3f0924dc-4a42-4935-838b-\
0924de78c9b1"],

Cell[TextData[{
 "Symbolic Integrity: The compiler handles index valence, canonicalization, \
and contraction via the ",
 StyleBox["ContractAll", "Input"],
 " and ",
 StyleBox["EvaluateUDPartials", "Input"],
 " functions. "
}], "Item",
 CellChangeTimes->{
  3.9782267679447403`*^9, {3.978227017829777*^9, 3.978227188189443*^9}, {
   3.978227320836319*^9, 3.978227362157029*^9}, 
   3.978228646150115*^9},ExpressionUUID->"e59cbd14-4a66-4b35-b9c2-\
36f563a9d321"],

Cell["\<\
Algebraic Simplification: The toolkit generates the Riemann and Ricci tensors \
and decouples the vacuum field equations.\
\>", "Item",
 CellChangeTimes->{
  3.9782267679447403`*^9, {3.978227017829777*^9, 3.978227196292163*^9}, {
   3.978227371604761*^9, 
   3.978227411306007*^9}},ExpressionUUID->"bab6601f-3a4f-4941-b60a-\
b0861bd43c23"],

Cell["\<\
Ground Truth Verification: The final derived solution, matches the standard \
result in the Wolfram Function Repository exactly.\
\>", "Item",
 CellChangeTimes->{
  3.9782267679447403`*^9, {3.978227017829777*^9, 3.978227201899907*^9}, {
   3.978227413848699*^9, 
   3.978227428915608*^9}},ExpressionUUID->"b0fcf2b4-64a3-48dc-876a-\
852158a2a16a"],

Cell[CellGroupData[{

Cell["Limitations", "Subsection",
 CellChangeTimes->{{3.978227437148188*^9, 
  3.978227442161578*^9}},ExpressionUUID->"3097d5f5-b47c-4ddf-8aa4-\
0e4397f86a14"],

Cell["\<\
The current implementation operates as a script in the Global namespace. A \
future iteration (v2.0) will encapsulate the toolkit into a Wolfram Package \
to sanitize the namespace and offer a cleaner API. \
\>", "Text",
 CellChangeTimes->{
  3.9782267679447403`*^9, {3.978227017829777*^9, 3.978227273558428*^9}, 
   3.978227308415905*^9},ExpressionUUID->"ed6405e3-7a30-4fd1-8b7f-\
45d75c5bc94a"]
}, Open  ]],

Cell[CellGroupData[{

Cell["Future Notebooks", "Subsection",
 CellChangeTimes->{{3.978227446699684*^9, 
  3.978227452339609*^9}},ExpressionUUID->"6d1a6b27-cd56-4914-ba80-\
6cd8c6787cc0"],

Cell["\<\
With the engine now validated against the Schwarzschild solution, future \
notebooks will apply it to more complex geometries, including the computation \
of the Kretschmann scalar for physical singularities and the derivation of \
geodesic equations for orbital mechanics.\
\>", "Text",
 CellChangeTimes->{
  3.9782267679447403`*^9, {3.978227017829777*^9, 
   3.978227295373459*^9}},ExpressionUUID->"d94bddeb-278c-49a0-b335-\
2cce31ccea0d"]
}, Open  ]]
}, Open  ]],

